<title>INDIA: India approves Becton Dickinson investment.</title>
<headline>India approves Becton Dickinson investment.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian Industry Ministry said on Wednesday that it approved a 1.05-billion-rupee investment by U.S.-based Becton Dickinson and Co in a wholly-owned needle and syringe subsidiary.  </p>
<p>The investment was among 58 proposals worth a total of 6.6 billion rupees which were approved by the Foreign Investment Promotion Board, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
